From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:42:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: snapshot byte-valued character diagnostics for
 consumer rendering

Preserve existing ASCII database-prefix %c diagnostics as STRING values without producer formatting. Copy the byte before enqueue; do not interpret it as a Unicode code point. The AST converter accepts only the unchanged original argument in a direct LogChar Field, rejecting width/length changes, rewritten bytes and integer substitutions.

Checks: /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/test_convert.py (17 cases); same interpreter test/lint/lint-log-events.py --self-test (13 cases); git diff --check. Added actual native JSON/text escaping and lifetime controls; native execution remains pending the next combined gate.
